# Command dtach

## What does this command do:

A simple program that emulates the detach feature of screen

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: sudo dnf install dtach
For Raspberry Pi install using: sudo apt install dtach
For Mac install using: brew install dtach
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: sudo dnf install dtach

## Command path

For Fedora run: /usr/bin/dtach
For Raspberry Pi run: /usr/bin/dtach
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/dtach
For Mac container run: /usr/bin/dtach

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/crigler/dtach

## Command options

# Create a new session (or attach if socket exists), running <cmd>
dtach -A <socket> <cmd>

# Attach to an existing session only
dtach -a <socket>

# Create a new session (never attaches to an existing one)
dtach -c <socket> <cmd>

# Pipe mode: send stdin to session without scanning for detach character
dtach -p <socket>

# Set a custom detach character (default: Ctrl-\)
dtach -A <socket> <cmd> -e '^A'

# Disable the detach character entirely
dtach -A <socket> <cmd> -E

# Disable Ctrl-Z suspend handling
dtach -A <socket> <cmd> -z

# Set the redraw method: none, ctrl_l (default), or winch
dtach -A <socket> <cmd> -r winch

# Run in foreground (don't background the master process)
dtach -A <socket> <cmd> -N
